{"entries":[{"name":"羽柴壮一","reading":"はしばそういち","category":"character","keys":["羽柴壮一","壮一君","おにいさま","長男"],"content":"The eldest son of 羽柴壮太郎. As a teenager he was an adventurous boy who wanted to start a business in the South Seas, but his father refused, so he left home about ten years ago by stowaway on a small sailing ship. He later became a rubber plantation owner near Sandakan on Borneo, and he wrote to his father about three months before the story, asking to come home and apologize. He is about thirty, with a moustache, and is expected to return by plane via Shimonoseki. He arrives at Haneda Airport, where the whole family meets him; he is stylishly dressed in a brown overcoat and a double-breasted suit, is tanned, and looks like his photographs but even more handsome. He rides in a car between his parents, and at dinner that evening he tells stories of the South Seas and of his childhood."},{"name":"羽柴壮二","reading":"はしばそうじ","category":"character","keys":["羽柴壮二","壮二","壮二君"],"content":"The younger brother of 壮一 and a son of 羽柴壮太郎. He is still an elementary school pupil. He is looking forward to 壮一's return along with the rest of the family. On the morning of 壮一's arrival he suddenly appears from the 羽柴家の土蔵, an event that is presented as mysterious. At the airport he rides in a second car with 羽柴早苗 and 近藤老人, watching his brother through the rear window with growing happiness. At dinner 壮一 recalls that as a toddler the boy had gotten ink on his face after overturning an ink bottle in his older brother's study."},{"name":"羽柴壮太郎","reading":"はしばそうたろう","category":"character","keys":["羽柴壮太郎","壮太郎氏","羽柴氏","おとうさま","主人"],"content":"Business leader (実業界の大立者) and head of the Hashiba family, who lives in a large mansion in Azabu. He is the father of 壮一, 早苗 and 壮二. He had opposed his eldest son's wish to go to the South Seas, and the son ran away from home ten years ago. He keeps the six Romanov diamonds in a safe in his study, and he remains calm when he receives the thief's threatening notice. He welcomes 壮一 home at Haneda Airport and rides with him in the car. During the family dinner a telegram arrives from 二十面相 reading that the thief will come at midnight to collect the promised item; after reading it he falls silent, then warns the children that they must be very careful that night."},{"name":"羽柴早苗","reading":"はしばさなえ","category":"character","keys":["羽柴早苗","早苗","おねえさま"],"content":"A daughter of 羽柴壮太郎 and the older sister of 壮二 and 壮一. She goes to the airport with the family and rides in a car with 壮二 and 近藤老人 to meet and return with the returning 壮一."},{"name":"近藤老人","reading":"こんどうろうじん","category":"character","keys":["近藤老人","近藤支配人","支配人"],"content":"The steward (支配人) of the Hashiba household. When the threatening notice arrives, he reacts strongly, going to the police for protection and buying a fierce guard dog. He arranges for off-duty policemen to be called in turn so that two or three officers are always in the mansion. He goes to Haneda Airport to receive 壮一, riding in the second car with 壮二 and 早苗."},{"name":"二十面相","reading":"にじゅうめんそう","category":"character","keys":["二十面相","怪盗","賊","余","二〇"],"content":"A notorious thief (怪盗) who sends a threatening notice to 羽柴壮太郎 announcing that he will take the six large Romanov diamonds, which he claims to have obtained without payment. He gives no exact date, only warning that the Hashiba family should be very careful. The notice shows that he knows exactly where the diamonds are kept, in the study safe. On the evening of 壮一's return he sends a telegram to the Hashiba household, signed 二〇, saying that he will come at twelve o'clock tonight to collect the promised item."},{"name":"羽柴家の土蔵","reading":"はしばけのどぞう","category":"place","keys":["土蔵","羽柴家の土蔵"],"content":"A storehouse on the Hashiba family grounds. On the morning of 壮一's arrival, 壮二 suddenly emerges from it, an event that is presented as mysterious."},{"name":"羽田空港","reading":"はねだくうこう","category":"place","keys":["羽田空港","羽田"],"content":"The airport where 壮一 lands after returning from the South Seas. The whole Hashiba family goes there in the afternoon to meet him, arriving by car."}]}
